under","H4390":"to fill","H2651":"palm","H1513":"coal","H784":"fire","H2236":"to scatter","H5892":"excitement","H5869":"eye","H5975":"stand","H3225":"right","H1004":"place","H6051":"cloud","H853":"[Obj.]","H2691":"court","H6442":"inner","H7311":"to exalt","H3519":"glory","H3068":"LORD","H4670":"threshold","H5051":"brightness","H6963":"voice","H3671":"wing","H8085":"hear","H5704":"till","H2435":"outer","H410":"God","H7706":"Almighty","H1696":"speak","H1961":"to be","H6680":"to command","H3947":"take","H681":"beside","H212":"wheel","H7971":"depart","H3027":"hand","H5375":"raise","H5414":"give","H3318":"come","H8403":"pattern","H120":"man","H702":"four","H259":"one","H8658":"jasper","H8432":"midst","H3212":"to walk","H7253":"fourth","H3808":"not","H5437":"turn","H3588":"for","H4725":"place","H6437":"to turn","H310":"after","H3605":"all","H1320":"flesh","H1354":"back/rim/brow","H4392":"full","H5439":"around","H7121":"call to","H241":"ear","H6440":"before","H8145":"second","H7992":"third","H738":"lion","H7243":"fourth","H5404":"eagle","H7426":"be exalted","H1931":"he/she/it","H2416":"alive","H5104":"River","H3529":"Chebar","H776":"country/planet","H1571":"also","H1992":"they(masc.)","H7307":"spirit","H4480":"from","H5980":"close","H6607":"entrance","H8179":"gate","H6931":"eastern","H430":"God","H3478":"Israel","H4605":"above","H3045":"to know","H5676":"beside"},"ccc":{},"cccp":{},"com":[["challoner",11,null,"challoner","By four ways.... That is, by any of the four ways, forward, backward, to the right or to the left."],["challoner",13,null,"challoner","Voluble.... That is, rolling wheels, galgal."],["haydock",1,null,"haydock","Throne. It was a sky blue crystal or sapphire colour, (chap. i. 22, 26.) and was now empty, chap. i. The Lord spoke from the temple door, ver. 4. (Haydock)"],["haydock",2,null,"haydock","Out, to purify (St. Jerome) or punish the city, (Theodoret) which would shortly be reduced to ashes. (Vatable) (Menochius)"],["haydock",3,null,"haydock","Right, south of the priests’ court."],["haydock",4,null,"haydock","Lifted up, before chap. ix. 3. (Calmet) — A man seemed to be on the throne, (Worthington) or rather over the door of the holy place."],["haydock",5,null,"haydock","Court of the people. — Speaking in thunder."],["haydock",8,null,"haydock","Wings. They would seem to be distinct, or (Calmet) fingers appeared at the end of the wings. (Grotius)"],["haydock",9,null,"haydock","Stone. Hebrew Tharsis. Symmachus, “Hyacinth.” (Chap. i. 16.) (Calmet)"],["haydock",11,null,"haydock","By four ways. That is, by any of the four ways, forward, backward, to the right, or to the left. (Challoner) (Worthington)"],["haydock",12,null,"haydock","Wheels. These, as well as (Haydock) the cherubim, (Theodoret) were full of eyes. (Calmet)"],["haydock",13,null,"haydock","Voluble. That is, rolling wheels: galgal, (Challoner) which means “rolling:” (Haydock) or “he said to the wheels, Turn around about.” (Theodoret) — This is the real import of Hebrew. (Calmet) — Protestants have, “O wheel.” (Haydock)"],["haydock",14,null,"haydock","Cherub, or “ox.” All four seem to have had the resemblance of a man, but one more than the rest, which had respectively the appearance rather of an ox, a lion, or an eagle: (Worthington) or the ox was predominant in all, as both the head and feet were of it; (Calmet) which, however, does not constitute the greatest part, chap. i. 5. (Haydock)"],["haydock",15,null,"haydock","Creature. What I saw, was properly called cherubim. Charab, in Syriac means “to labour;” (Spencer) or cherubim may imply any composed and unusual figure, or “mixture,” Exodus xxv. 18. (Calmet) — Ezechiel being a priest, saw that the creatures resembled the cherubim of the temple. (Tirinus)"],["haydock",17,null,"haydock","Life. They were not mere machines; (Haydock) or they were pushed forward by an impetuous wind."],["haydock",19,null,"haydock","East gate, leading from the city to the court of the people. (Calmet) — How unwilling is this good father to leave his house! (Tirinus)"],["haydock",20,null,"haydock","Creature. The cherubim and all the throne seemed alive. (Haydock)"],["haydock",22,null,"haydock","Forward, thus shewing God’s decree to abandon the synagogue. (Tirinus)"]],"au":{"challoner":["Richard Challoner",0,0,1781,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/03566a.htm"],"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"]}}